  "body": "- [x] I license this and all my future contributions to Slint under the [MIT-0 license](https://opensource.org/license/mit-0). They are my own work, and no third party (such as my employer) holds rights to them.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis PR lets a `FocusScope` act as an input method (IME) client. That way, custom editing surfaces like rich text editors or code editors drawn with custom code can get composition events directly.\r\n\r\nFocusing an enabled `FocusScope` triggers the platform's input method (`TextInputInterface.text-input-focused: true`), while losing focus cleanly disables it.\r\n\r\n## New API\r\n\r\n```slint\r\nscope := FocusScope {\r\n    // When true, enables the scope to act as an IME client\r\n    accepts-text-input: true;\r\n\r\n    // Tracked properties synchronized with the input method automatically:\r\n    ime-text: \"hello\";\r\n    ime-cursor-position: 5;\r\n    ime-cursor-rect-x: 10px;\r\n    ime-cursor-rect-y: 20px;\r\n    ime-cursor-rect-width: 1px;\r\n    ime-cursor-rect-height: 14px;\r\n\r\n    composition-update(event) => {\r\n        // Display event.text as pre-edit (marked) text at the caret\r\n        scope.ime-preedit-text = event.text;\r\n        accept\r\n    }\r\n    composition-commit(event) => {\r\n        // Insert event.text at the caret\r\n        scope.ime-preedit-text = \"\";\r\n        accept\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### New Properties & Callbacks\r\n\r\n* **`accepts-text-input`** (_in property \\<bool>_): Enables the scope to accept text composition events. Note that toggling this while the scope already holds focus has no effect until focus is lost and regained.\r\n* **`ime-text`** (_in property \\<string>_): Text context surrounding the caret, excluding pre-edit text.\r\n* **`ime-cursor-position`** (_in property \\<int>_): The caret position in bytes within `ime-text`.\r\n* **`ime-anchor-position`** (_in property \\<int>_): Selection anchor position in bytes.\r\n* **`ime-has-anchor`** (_in property \\<bool>_): Flag indicating if a selection anchor is currently active.\r\n* **`ime-preedit-text`** (_in property \\<string>_): The current pre-edit composition text.\r\n* **`ime-preedit-offset`** (_in property \\<int>_): The byte offset of the pre-edit text within `ime-text`.\r\n* **`ime-cursor-rect-x` / `-y` / `-width` / `-height`** (_in property \\<length>_): Defines the local caret bounding box, allowing correct orientation and placement of the OS candidate windows.\r\n* **`ime-input-type`** (_in property \\<InputType>_): Set type hints (e.g., text, number, password) for virtual/on-screen keyboards.\r\n* **`ime-input-method-hints`** (_in property \\<InputMethodHints>_): Controls behavioral adjustments like capitalization, auto-correct, and auto-complete.\r\n* **`composition-update(CompositionEvent)`** (_callback_): Fires whenever the input method alters the composition pre-edit text sequence.\r\n* **`composition-commit(CompositionEvent)`** (_callback_): Fires when final text composition is committed.\r\n\r\n### New Structs\r\n\r\n#### `CompositionEvent`\r\n* **`text`** (_string_)\r\n* **`preedit-selection-start`** (_int_)\r\n* **`preedit-selection-end`** (_int_)\r\n* **`replacement-range-start`** (_int_)\r\n* **`replacement-range-end`** (_int_)\r\n* **`cursor-position`** (_int_)\r\n* **`anchor-position`** (_int_)\r\n",
